; SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later AND CC-BY-SA-4.0
; buffet.source.vla - Buffet, all you can sheet: an idle game in which you run an
; asset-management firm, and a spreadsheet you are allowed to open (OMAKASE.md). The pass
; expands this file into buffet.vla beside it, the rows the engine loads (SPEC.md section
; 7.8): edit this one, then expand it again with
;   cargo run --release --example expand
; and the oracle's tests hold the cartridge to this file and every frame of it to the
; game written by hand, oracle/src/buffet.rs.
;
; Course 0 is being cooked, a dish at a time (OMAKASE.md, COURSE.0). Served so far:
;   POT.1   the calendar and the dice: the Day sheet, the one sheet that reads the frame,
;           and the Dice sheet, the market's die, which rolls once a market day, and the
;           exam's, which rolls once a game.
;
; The market's clock (BD-7). One tick is one market day, thirty frames at the manifest's
; rate of thirty, so a day a second and a year about six minutes. The Day sheet alone
; reads the frame, Clock!B1; every other formula reads the day, so that a frame between
; two days computes the calendar's three cells, the day, the phase and the boundary, and
; nothing else, and a day's first frame computes what the day moves. The Clock's rate is
; the teacher's dial: written to 60, the game runs two days a second and no formula
; changes, since the frames a day stay thirty.
;
; The dice (BD-3). The market is a pure function of the seed and the day, so its die
; steps on a day's first frame and on no other, from the seed on the first day, and the
; same days give the same dice however many frames a day there are. Each day the die
; jumps 1,017 draws, and the day's draws stand beneath it, so a dish that needs a draw
; takes the next free one, and a later course adds draws without moving one an earlier
; course reads. The exam's die is the seed jumped half the generator's period away, so
; the market and the exam never share a die: the market's die reaches the exam's after
; more than a million days. Each jump is a multiplier below 2^22, so every product stays
; under 2^53 and exact in a double, as Park and Miller's own step is.

; The libraries whose macros this source calls, both beside it: the kit, Alonzo's
; common.vla copied at the pin (sheets, labels, on, cells, formulas and hold), then
; Buffet's own, kitchen.vla (draws).
(include "common.vla")
(include "kitchen.vla")

(cartridge "buffet"
  (spec 3)
  (title "Buffet")
  (rate 30)
  (screen grid 80 50)
  (seed 777)
  (author "Spreadsheet Company")
  (license "AGPL-3.0-or-later AND CC-BY-SA-4.0")
  (notes "Buffet: all you can sheet. The kitchen is open and the dining room is not: so far the market's calendar, a market day a second, and its dice, rolled once a day where anyone can watch them roll. Pick the Day or the Dice sheet to watch."))

(sheets "Screen" "Day" "Dice")

; ---- POT.1: the calendar ------------------------------------------------------------
; A block of settings and its workings, a label in column A beside each value in B. The
; frame is 1 in the first step, so the day and the phase count from the frame less one:
; the first frame is the first day's first, and every day, the first too, opens on a
; boundary frame and holds thirty frames.

(on "Day"
  (labels "A1" "frames a day" "days a year" "day" "phase" "boundary" "year" "day of the year")
  (cells
    ("B1" 30)                       ; frames a day: the manifest's rate, a day a second; a test holds the two equal
    ("B2" 365))                     ; days a year: every day a market day, weekends and holidays too
  (formulas
    ("B3" "=INT((Clock!B1-1)/B1)")  ; the day, from 0: the market's clock, which every other formula reads
    ("B4" "=MOD(Clock!B1-1,B1)")    ; the phase: the frame within the day, from 0
    ("B5" "=IF(B4=0,1,0)")          ; the boundary: 1 in a day's first frame, the one frame the market moves in
    ("B6" "=INT(B3/B2)+1")          ; the year, from 1
    ("B7" "=MOD(B3,B2)+1")))        ; the day of the year, from 1 to 365

; ---- POT.1: the dice ----------------------------------------------------------------
; Two streams, each a die and its draws, the draws by the library's verb. Column C
; holds each draw's uniform; columns E and F the two jumps, each in draws and as the
; multiplier that makes it, 16807 to that power modulo 2147483647, which a test holds.

(on "Dice"
  (labels "A1" "the market's die" "draw 1" "draw 2" "draw 3" "draw 4")
  (cells ("C1" "uniform"))
  (hold                             ; the market's die, the stream's state:
    "B1"                            ;   its cell
    "Day!$B$5=1"                    ;   when it rolls: a day's first frame, and no other
    "MOD(IF(Day!$B$3=0,Clock!$B$3,Dice.last!B1)*$F$2,2147483647)")   ; what it rolls to: the seed on the first day, else yesterday's die, jumped a day's draws
  (draws                            ; the market's draws, read by the dish that needs one:
    "B2"                            ;   the first, beneath the die
    4)                              ;   how many a day so far: POT.2's four phases read them first
  (labels "A7" "the exam's die" "draw 1" "draw 2")
  (cells ("C7" "uniform"))
  (formulas
    ("B7" "=MOD(Clock!$B$3*$F$4,2147483647)"))   ; the exam's die: the seed jumped half the period, once a game
  (draws                            ; the exam's draws:
    "B8"                            ;   the first, beneath its die
    2)                              ;   how many: GUARD.1's start and stride through the bank
  (labels "E1" "a day's jump, in draws" "its multiplier" "the exam's jump, in draws" "its multiplier")
  (cells
    ("F1" 1017)                     ; a day's jump: the first past a thousand whose multiplier is below 2^22
    ("F2" 86383)                    ; 16807^1017 modulo 2147483647
    ("F3" 1073741912)               ; the exam's jump: 2^30 + 88, the first past half the period whose multiplier is below 2^22
    ("F4" 1164196)))                ; 16807^1073741912 modulo 2147483647
